From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:38:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Advertise soft faults by default

fault_control=3 has been the default since Oct 7. The Mesa soft-fault
bugs that kept this off are fixed (hk robust UBOs 243c5ac0c43, strict
sparse residency 31b9d1d5bfb). On #144 with Mesa 1ecf668, soft_faults=1
showed 0 G16 fault lines over 2x Lethal and 2x Dota (Lethal 31.7/31.9
vs 31.2/31.2 fps). Requires that Mesa on every device's system driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
index 1d05e7ed5a92..00f57a04fa42 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/asahi_m4.rs
@@ -277,8 +277,8 @@ fn probe<'bound>(
             description: "Firmware fault control word (region C +0xe28): 3 as macOS; 0 hard faults",
         },
         soft_faults: u32 {
-            default: 0,
-            description: "Debug: 1 advertises soft faults to userspace (needs fault_control=3)",
+            default: 1,
+            description: "1 advertises soft faults to userspace (needs fault_control=3; Mesa with hk 243c5ac0c43 and 31b9d1d5bfb); 0 hides them",
         },
     },
 }
